      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{65f4b1a3d0a7a0c657a7d3a8|full_name} The warning is still triggered by the vrcsdk. It can be avoided by adding to the array where needed rather than resizing ahead of time, or by using a placeholder object when resizing (since the physbone logic replaces it all later anyways).\n\nI don't believe the linked unity issue is actually related, because that's a report of unity itself triggering the warning from one of its own internal bone systems, and it was already patched in the U6 editor release we're using now.",
